The layer-2 control variate looks worthwhile enough to try in the candidate: it uses only the supplied weights, gives a consistent small gain in synthetic tests, and the extra cost is mostly fixed per MLP. I’m going to patch `submission.py` with cached pre-whitened directions, a budget formula for prediction-time work, and the blended layer-2 correction.
